                <pb facs="0485" n="473" xml:id="pg473"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/4407: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Barcelona</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Perkins</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Barcelona</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-01-18T12:00:00+00:00">January 18,
                        1937—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Yesterday personally observed contingent of American, German and English
                    volunteers. Americans numbering about 40 headed the column and carried a red
                    flag marked American battalion.</p>
                <p>As circumstances may render advisable statutes named in the Department’s January
                    13, 7 p.m., will be brought to the attention of American citizens.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
